    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0512" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/3–1847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-18T17:00:00+03:00">March 18, 1947—5
                            [p.m.?]</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 18—12:28 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>860. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kosmos</hi> 1.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d411-f1"/>
                    Your 532 of 4 p.m., 15 March refers. In view of exchange of letters between
                    Molotov and myself, I suggest the last paragraph of your proposed memorandum to
                    Soviet Government, which starts “the Soviet Government in its note”, and ends
                    “detachment of marines at Tsingtao” be deleted. In its place I suggest a
                    statement substantially as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“With regard to the matter of US troops in China, this will be <pb
                                facs="0513" n="503" xml:id="pg503"/> covered in the exchange of
                            information referred to in the communication of the Secretary of State
                            dated 15 March.”<anchor n="52" xml:id="d411-f2"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I will advise Embassy here when you indicate clearance.</p>
                <p>New subject: I have discussed and given a copy of the last paragraph of your 509
                    of 8 p.m., 13 March<anchor n="53" xml:id="d411-f3"/> with Mr. Bevin.<anchor
                        n="54" xml:id="d411-f4"/> He is taking the matter up by cable with
                    London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d411-f1" n="51" xml:id="d411-f1-content">
